# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# intercom-go build artifacts and local-only config (001.001.001-ST)
dist/
.env.*
config.toml

# Preserve-only machine-local paths (011.001-T, resolves 9F9A3CB2 item: confirmed
# NOT previously ignored). These carry per-machine command/environment payloads
# and are never intended for commit; ignored individually (not directory-wide) so
# unrelated content under the same parent directories remains trackable.
.claude/instructions.md
.github/copilot/settings.local.json
.autoharness/gates/pipeline-topology-force-audit.log
.backlogit/hooks_queue.jsonl

# Copilot tracking, Test output and PR comments
.test-output.txt
.test-out.txt
*.pr-comments.json
.pr-comments.json
.copilot-tracking/pr/**/pr-reference.xml
*.code-workspace

# Directories
bin/
logs/
.vscode/
.copilot/
.mcp.json

# Local environment files (secrets) — never commit. Only .env.example may be tracked.
.env
!.env.example

# Plugin .mcp.json is intentionally tracked (distinct from local dev config).
# 011.015-T credential check: if plugin/.mcp.json is ever actually tracked,
# it MUST reference credentials by ${VAR} indirection only (never a literal
# secret value) -- the existing CI `security` job's unconditional
# `gitleaks detect --source . --no-git -v` scan (which covers every file
# present on disk, respecting no ignore rules under --no-git) is the
# durable, standing safeguard over this and every other newly-un-ignored
# path here; neither plugin/.mcp.json nor .env.example exists in this
# repo as of this commit, so there is nothing to scan yet.
!plugin/.mcp.json

# Ephemeral SQLite databases (always regenerated; never commit)
backlogit.db
.backlogit/backlogit.db
.backlogit/backlogit.db-shm
.backlogit/backlogit.db-wal
.backlogit/checkpoints/
.backlogit/runtime/

# Runtime state (per-consumer checkpoints, not committed)
.autoharness/staging/
.autoharness/backups/
prompt.md

# Advisory file locks (autoharness concurrency protocol)
.*.lock

# Machine-local telemetry harvest checkpoint (changes per machine/run)
.backlogit/.telemetry-checkpoint.json

# Engram runtime data (keep templates/, registry.yaml, .version).
# 011.015-T effect assertion (NOT assumed): the four negations immediately
# below are INERT under git semantics -- git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is already excluded by ".engram/" above. Verified
# via `git check-ignore -v` for each: all four resolve to the ".engram/"
# directory-pattern match (line above), never their own negation line, so
# .version/.workspace-id/config.toml/registry.yaml under .engram/ remain
# IGNORED despite these lines existing. Recorded here rather than shipping
# a silently-wrong ignore policy as "validated".
.engram/
!.engram/.version
!.engram/.workspace-id
!.engram/config.toml
!.engram/registry.yaml

# graphtor-docs — managed by graphtor-docs install
.graphtor/
diff.txt

# Ephemeral depguard fixture directories created transiently by
# scripts/check-depguard-fixtures.sh and removed by its own trap cleanup;
# ignored as a belt-and-suspenders control so an abnormal termination that
# bypasses shell trap handling (SIGKILL, CI runner hard-stop) can never
# leave these deliberately-non-compliant fixture files stageable via a
# careless `git add -A` (security review + constitution review finding,
# shipment 010-S).
internal/depguardfixture/
internal/copilotprobe2/
